<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Experience the very best of China in one extraordinary 12-day journey. From the imperial grandeur of Beijing's Forbidden City to the adorable giant pandas of Chengdu, the otherworldly sandstone pillars of Zhangjiajie, and the glittering skyline of Shanghai — this tour is China's greatest hits album. Perfect as a Silk Road extension or standalone adventure.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Walk the Great Wall at Mutianyu</li><li>Explore the Forbidden City & Tiananmen Square</li>
      <li>Meet giant pandas at Chengdu Research Base</li>
      <li>Hike Zhangjiajie's Avatar Mountains</li>
      <li>Walk the world's longest glass bridge</li>
      <li>Admire Shanghai's Bund & Pudong skyline</li>
      <li>Savor Sichuan hotpot & Beijing roast duck</li>
      <li>Ride the world's fastest train: Shanghai Maglev</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Beijing</h4><p>Airport pickup and transfer to your 4-star hotel. Evening welcome dinner featuring authentic Beijing roast duck at a historic restaurant.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Beijing 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Beijing — Tiananmen & Forbidden City</h4><p>Morning at Tiananmen Square, the world's largest public square. Spend the afternoon exploring the Forbidden City — 980 buildings, 9,999 rooms, 500 years of imperial history. Evening stroll through Wangfujing Night Market.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Beijing 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Beijing — Great Wall at Mutianyu</h4><p>Journey to the Mutianyu section of the Great Wall — less crowded, beautifully restored, with stunning mountain views. Take the cable car up and toboggan down! Afternoon visit to the Summer Palace.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Beijing 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Beijing — Temple of Heaven & Hutong</h4><p>Morning at the Temple of Heaven where locals practice tai chi. Rickshaw ride through traditional hutong alleys with a family visit. Afternoon flight to Chengdu (2.5 hrs).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Chengdu 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Chengdu — Pandas!</h4><p>Early start to the Chengdu Research Base of Giant Panda Breeding — watch pandas at their most active during breakfast. Afternoon at Jinli Ancient Street and a traditional Sichuan tea house.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Chengdu 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Chengdu — Leshan Giant Buddha</h4><p>Day trip to Leshan to see the world's largest stone Buddha (71m tall), carved into a cliff face in the 8th century. Evening Sichuan hotpot dinner — the real deal!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Chengdu 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Chengdu &#9992; Zhangjiajie</h4><p>Morning flight to Zhangjiajie (1.5 hrs). Afternoon visit to Tianmen Mountain — ride the world's longest cable car and walk the famous glass skywalk clinging to a cliff face.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Zhangjiajie 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangjiajie National Forest Park</h4><p>Full day in the park that inspired Avatar's floating mountains. Hike the Golden Whip Stream, take the Bailong Elevator (world's tallest outdoor lift), and explore Yuanjiajie's panoramic viewpoints.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Zhangjiajie 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangjiajie — Grand Canyon & Glass Bridge</h4><p>Walk across the world's longest and highest glass-bottomed bridge spanning the Grand Canyon. Afternoon at Baofeng Lake for a tranquil boat ride. Evening flight to Shanghai.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Shanghai 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Shanghai — The Bund & Pudong</h4><p>Morning at the Bund promenade with views of colonial architecture and Pudong's futuristic skyline. Visit Yu Garden, a 16th-century masterpiece. Afternoon at Shanghai Tower (632m) observation deck.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Shanghai 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Shanghai — Free Day</h4><p>Free day to explore at your own pace. Options: French Concession walking tour, Shanghai Museum, Propaganda Poster Art Centre, or shopping on Nanjing Road. Ride the Maglev train to Pudong Airport (431 km/h)!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Shanghai 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Shanghai</h4><p>Airport transfer for your departure flight. Take home memories of China's greatest hits. &#20877;&#35265;!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

